rway is a significant contributor to international health and research initiatives. It provided data for the World Health Organization's (WHO) international growth reference patterns for children, aiding in the establishment of global health standards. Additionally, Norway is one of the five northern European countries that played a crucial role in the formation of the Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) group, which focuses on improving surgical recovery protocols. Through these contributions, Norway demonstrates its commitment to advancing health and medical practices on an international scale.", "NETHERLANDS:The Netherlands is one of the five northern European countries that contributed to the establishment of the ERAS group.", "MULTIMODAL REHABILITATION:Multimodal rehabilitation refers to the combination of various interventions aimed at improving recovery outcomes for patients undergoing surgery.", "PERIOPERATIVE CARE:Perioperative care encompasses the care provided before, during, and after surgery, which is crucial for patient recovery.", "FAST-TRACK SURGERY:Fast-track surgery is a term used to describe surgical protocols designed to expedite recovery and reduce hospital stay.", "DUODENOPANCREATECTOMY:Duodenopancreatectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of both the duodenum and the pancreas. This procedure is often discussed in the context of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols, which aim to improve recovery outcomes for patients. Additionally, duodenopancreatectomy necessitates careful nutritional management to support the patient's recovery and overall health following the surgery.", "RECTAL SURGERY:Rectal surgery encompasses surgical procedures performed on the rectum, which may incorporate Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols to enhance patient outcomes. These protocols are designed to optimize recovery and improve overall surgical results, making rectal surgery a critical component of modern surgical practices.", "MORBIDITY:Morbidity refers to the condition of being diseased or the incidence of illness, encompassing the presence of disease or medical conditions that affect health and quality of life. It is a critical focus for initiatives like Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS), which aims to reduce morbidity through improved surgical protocols.", "ERAS:ERAS, which stands for Enhanced Recovery After Surgery, is a comprehensive set of recommendations designed to enhance the recovery process for patients following surgical procedures. Initially published in 2005 and updated in subsequent years, ERAS serves as a multimodal protocol specifically for elective colon surgery. The protocol focuses on improving patient outcomes by implementing various perioperative care strategies that facilitate a smoother and more efficient recovery.", "NUTRITION RISK SCREENING:Nutrition Risk Screening (NRS-2002) is one of the tools used to assess nutritional risk in patients undergoing major scheduled surgery."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}